  <!-- EN:
    <li>alienistBasis   ->When Humanity left its home planet, it found no alien life. A lonely Universe filled with nothing but unthinking matter.</li>
    <li>alienistBasis   ->If we are not alone in the Universe, our neighbours are certainly too far away to affect us. We have found no new life beyond the one we carried from Old Earth.</li>
    <li>alienistBasis   ->Humanity has found no "true" alien life in the Universe. No strange new creatures beyond simple, unicellular bacteria in the deepest oceanic trenches and a few self-replicating amino acids in some remote asteroid belt.</li>
    <li>alienistBasis   ->Upon leaving Earth, we stumbled upon a hostile Universe devoid of all life but our own.</li>
    <li>alienistFact    ->This didn't stop our ancestors from creating new beings. Exotic, alien life derived from terrestrial genomes to populate the myriad worlds of human space.</li>
    <li>alienistFact    ->Our ingenuity, however, was far greater. We twisted and tangled the genetic strains carried by our forefathers from Earth, turning ancient breeds into new, wondrous creatures.</li>
    <li>alienistFact    ->Human creativity was not to be shackled by this unfortunate constraint, and we warped the ancient genomes of Earth creatures into all sorts of new animals. Amazing creations.</li>
    <li>alienistFact    ->However, playing God is what humans excel at. Like versatile clay we molded the ancient genelines into astonishing new creatures. Genetic marvels to populate an empty Universe.</li>
    <li>alienistProphecy->[itIsSaid] we will learn more about these creatures, and we will unlock secrets that will allow us to prosper on the Rim.</li>
    <li>itIsSaid->With careful experimentation,</li>
    <li>itIsSaid->Either through technology or more arcane means</li>
    <li>itIsSaid->Many techniques behind their creation have been lost with time, but in time</li>
  -->
  <AM_AlienismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <li>alienistBasis   ->当人类离开自己的家园后，没有发现任何异域生命。一个孤独的宇宙，除了没有思想的物质，什么都没有。</li>
    <li>alienistBasis   ->如果我们不是宇宙中的唯一，我们的邻居肯定离我们太远了，无法影响到我们。除了我们从古地球带来的生命外，我们没有发现任何新生命。</li>
    <li>alienistBasis   ->人类在宇宙中没有发现任何“真正的”异域生命。除了某些星球的海沟最深处中简单的单细胞细菌和在一些遥远的小行星带中发现的会自我复制的氨基酸之外，没有发现任何奇怪的新生物。</li>
    <li>alienistBasis   ->离开地球时，我们偶然发现我们所处在一个充满敌意的宇宙，除了我们自己及古地球的生命外，没有任何生命。</li>
    <li>alienistFact    ->这并没有阻止我们的祖先创造新的生命。使用古地球生物基因组造出来的“异域生命”，在人类的万千世界中繁衍生息。</li>
    <li>alienistFact    ->然而，我们的创造能力十分强大。我们扭曲和混乱了我们祖先从古地球上带来的生物基因组，把古地球生命变成了新的、奇妙的生物。</li>
    <li>alienistFact    ->人类的创造力不会被这种不幸的限制所束缚，我们将古地球生物的古老基因组扭曲成各种各样的新动物。这些造物简直惊为天人。</li>
    <li>alienistFact    ->然而，人类最擅长扮演上帝。就像多功能粘土一样，我们将古地球生物的古老基因组塑造成了令人惊讶的新生物。在一个空荡荡的宇宙中，基因创造了奇迹。</li>
    <li>alienistProphecy->[itIsSaid]我们将更多地了解这些生物，我们将揭开让我们在边缘世界繁荣的秘密。</li>
    <li>itIsSaid->经过仔细的实验，</li>
    <li>itIsSaid->通过科技或者更神秘的手段</li>
    <li>itIsSaid->随着时间的推移，他们进行基因工程的许多技术都已遗失，但那都是以前的事了，现在</li>
  </AM_AlienismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>

  <!-- EN:
    <li>lesson(priority=-1)->stuff happens</li>
    <li>r_pattern->"[r_atheismlessonIntro] [r_lesson]. [r_lessonReinforcement] [r_atheismlessonReinforcement]"\n\n  - [lessonAttribution]</li>
    <li>lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]'s [book] on [concept]</li>
    <li>book->lecture</li>
    <li>book->letter</li>
    <li>book->conference</li>
    <li>book->address</li>
    <li>book->discourse</li>
    <li>concept->the Death of God</li>
    <li>concept->Non-belief</li>
    <li>concept->Scepticism</li>
    <li>concept->Irreligion</li>
    <li>concept->Godlessness</li>
    <li>concept->the Rejection of Magical Thinking</li>
    <li>concept->Enlightened Humanism</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->... thus what is wanted are blindness and intoxication and an eternal song over the waves in which reason has drowned. The objective of religion is clear, hiding to us that</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->Human decency is not derived from religion. It precedes it. Once you understand that it becomes clear:</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->Atheism is more than just the knowledge that gods do not exist, and that religion is either a mistake or a fraud. Atheism is an attitude. It teaches us one thing:</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->Religion is excellent stuff for keeping common people quiet. The more controlled they are the longer it takes them to realize that</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->There is something infantile in the presumption that somebody else has a responsibility to give your life meaning and point. Only you can realize that</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->Being a Humanist means trying to behave decently without expectation of rewards or punishment after you are dead. You will show everyone that</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->When one person suffers from a delusion, it is called insanity. When many people suffer from a delusion it is called a Religion. Only those who are free from magical thinking can see that</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->I believe the simplest explanation is, there is no God. No one created the universe and no one directs our fate. This leads me to a profound realization that</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->We can judge our progress by the courage of our questions and the depth of our answers, our willingness to embrace what is true rather than what feels good.</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->The more I learn about the universe, the less convinced I am that there's any sort of benevolent force that has anything to do with it, at all.</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->After coming into contact with a religious man I always feel I must wash my hands.</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->I don't want to believe. I want to know.</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->With or without religion, good people can behave well and bad people can do evil; but for good people to do evil - that takes religion.</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->Civilization will not attain to its perfection until the last stone from the last church falls on the last priest.</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->We must question the story logic of having an all-knowing all-powerful God, who creates faulty Humans, and then blames them for his own mistakes.</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->If there is a God, atheism must seem to Him as less of an insult than religion.</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->When people ask me if a god created the universe, I tell them that the question itself makes no sense.</li>
    <li>lessonReinforcement->No one can argue with that.</li>
  -->
  <AM_AtheismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <li>lesson(priority=-1)->事情发生了</li>
    <li>r_pattern->“[r_atheismlessonIntro][r_lesson]。[r_lessonReinforcement][r_atheismlessonReinforcement]”\n\n  - [lessonAttribution]</li>
    <li>lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]，关于[concept]的[book]</li>
    <li>book->演讲</li>
    <li>book->信件</li>
    <li>book->会议</li>
    <li>book->演说</li>
    <li>book->论文</li>
    <li>concept->神明已死</li>
    <li>concept->无信仰</li>
    <li>concept->质疑宗教</li>
    <li>concept->无宗教</li>
    <li>concept->无神明</li>
    <li>concept->拒绝胡思乱想</li>
    <li>concept->提高人文素质</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->我们决不能被盲目与迷信的海浪淹没。宗教有着明确的目的，它向我们隐瞒了</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->人类的行为准则并非源自宗教。我希望你能理解这一点：</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->无神论并非只让我们意识到神明并不存在，它还揭发了宗教欺罔瞒骗的本质。无神论本身就是一种态度。它教会了我们一件事情：</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->宗教是让普通民众保持缄默的有效手段。他们越受宗教的控制，就越难意识到</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->让他人来赋予你生命的意义与目标，这听起来是否有些可笑呢？只有你自己能认识到</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->成为人文主义者意味着你想要的是得体的死亡，而不是期望因此得到奖惩。你会让大家都知道</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->当一个人被妄想蒙骗时，这叫做精神失常。当许多人被妄想蒙骗时，这叫做宗教。只有那些不胡思乱想的人才能认识到</li>
    <li>atheismlessonIntro->我相信最简单的解释就是，这世上没有神明。没有人创造了宇宙，也没有人引导我们的命运。这使我深刻地意识到</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->我们能通过发问的勇气与答案的深度来辨别自己是否有进步，我们愿意接纳真理，而不是那些自我感觉良好的东西。 </li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->我对宇宙了解的越多，就越不相信有神明的力量与它相关。</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->在和一名虔诚的信徒交流后，我总觉得应该好好洗洗手。</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->我不想去“相信”，我想亲自去理解。</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->无论宗教存在与否，好人会遵规守矩，坏人也会为非作歹；但，让好人为非作歹——这时就需要宗教的力量了。</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->直至最后一座教堂的最后一块砖瓦砸死最后一位神父，文明才能达到至臻之境。</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->我们必将对描述全知全能神明的故事逻辑提出质疑，祂故意创造出了不完美的人类，还要把自身的错误归咎于人类身上。</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->如果真的有神明存在的话，无神论对祂来说与其说是种侮辱，还不如说是一种宗教。</li>
    <li>atheismlessonReinforcement->当有人问我神明是否创造了宇宙时，我轻轻一笑，告诉他们这个问题毫无意义。</li>
    <li>lessonReinforcement->没人能反驳这一点。</li>
  </AM_AtheismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  
  <!-- EN:
    <li>lesson(priority=-1)->stuff happens</li>
