    <li>concept->the Brass Chronicles</li>
    <li>corsairlessonIntro->"Pillagin', shoutin' an' slashin' — that be how we sail! May she always be swabbin' an' riggin'." Our captain taught us that</li>
    <li>corsairlessonIntro->"A wise knave keeps only comp'ny with a pox-ridden rascal an' a grungy anchor." The boss preached that</li>
    <li>corsairlessonIntro->"Bucket o' bladder stench, ye blaggard! Did ye dance a jig on me scabbard?" - the captain said. Strife taught us one thing:</li>
    <li>corsairlessonIntro->"Begad! Why be they screamin' so cockeredly? I be broadsidin' on their bowspirit like a whoreson seadog!". The insane ramblings from the boss made us understand that</li>
    <li>corsairlessonIntro->"Damnation seize me soul if I give ye quarters, or take any from ye." The courage of the captain was showing us that</li>
