  <AM_CorsairDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <li>lesson(priority=-1)->事情发生了</li>
    <li>r_pattern->"[r_corsairlessonIntro][r_lesson]。[r_lessonReinforcement]"\n\n  - [lessonAttribution]</li>
    <li>lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]，关于[concept]的[book]</li>
    <li>book->演讲</li>
    <li>book->激昂演讲</li>
    <li>book->讲话</li>
    <li>book->动员</li>
    <li>book->抨击</li>
    <li>concept->劫掠</li>
    <li>concept->掠夺弱者</li>
    <li>concept->袭击</li>
    <li>concept->走跳板</li>
    <li>concept->坏血病</li>
    <li>concept->黄铜历代志</li>
    <li>corsairlessonIntro->“‘掠夺’、‘怒吼’和‘斩杀’——这就是我们海盗的生存方式！愿我们的航行一路顺利！”船长教导我们</li>
    <li>corsairlessonIntro->“一个有脑子的恶徒只能和浑身起疹的无赖与锈蚀肮脏的船锚为伴。”我们的头儿说</li>
    <li>corsairlessonIntro->“怎么有股尿骚味，你这小畜生！又想被我的剑捅的上蹿下跳了吗？”船长说。这些日常中的争吵教会了我们一件事情：</li>
    <li>corsairlessonIntro->“妈的！为什么他们叫的像公鸡打鸣一样？我现在就像是一个撞在船首斜桅上的混蛋水手一样！”头儿的胡乱叫骂让我们意识到</li>
    <li>corsairlessonIntro->“如果我接受了你们的投降或向你们摇尾乞怜，那我就是个该被千刀万剐的王八蛋！”英勇无畏的船长向我们证明了</li>
    <li>corsairlessonIntro->“我对你们来说是个恶徒，而你们对我来说就像克拉肯海怪一样！我是认真的！”我们完全没搞明白头儿在说些什么，但可以确信的是</li>
    <li>lessonReinforcement->没人能反驳这一点。</li>
  </AM_CorsairDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  
  <!-- EN:
    <li>lesson(priority=-1)->stuff happens</li>
    <li>r_pattern->"[r_jainistlessonIntro] [r_lesson]. [r_lessonReinforcement] [r_jainlessonReinforcement]"\n\n  - [lessonAttribution]</li>
    <li>lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]'s [revision] of the [book]</li>
    <li>lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]'s [revision] of the [book], [edition]</li>
    <li>lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]'s memorized sutras</li>
    <li>revision->interpretation</li>
    <li>revision->preserved meditations</li>
    <li>revision->theological musings</li>
    <li>revision->reflection</li>
    <li>revision->rumination</li>
    <li>book->teachings of Mahavira</li>
    <li>book->Agamas</li>
    <li>book->compiled sutras</li>
    <li>book->Purvas</li>
    <li>edition->32nd Edition</li>
    <li>edition->43rd Edition</li>
    <li>edition->52nd Edition</li>
    <li>edition->57th Edition</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->This is my country, that is your country; these are the conceptions of narrow souls - to the liberal minded the whole world is a family. I want you to understand:</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->In happiness and suffering, in joy and grief, we should regard all creatures as we regard our own self. This teaches us that</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->Some foolish men declare that a creator made the world. The doctrine that the world was created is ill advised and should be rejected. If God created the world, where was he before the creation? These musings did teach me one thing:</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->By teaching the sacred Agamas on the [place_summary] [place_name], I realized that</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->May peace rule the universe; may peace rule in kingdoms and empires; may peace rule in states and in the lands of the potentates; may peace rule in the house of friends and may peace also rule in the house of enemies. In peace you will realize that</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->We preach and practice brotherhood — not only of man but of all living beings — not on Sundays only but on all the days of the week. We believe in the law of universal justice. We preach that</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->If a person's mind is controlled by forces of revenge and jealousy, it cannot express love and sympathy. One thing will become increasingly clear then: that</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->A man is seated on top of a tree in the midst of a burning forest. He sees all living beings perish. But he doesn’t realize that the same fate is soon to overtake him also. That man is a fool. He needs to realize that</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->Attachment and aversion are the root cause of karma, and karma originates from infatuation. Karma is the root cause of birth and death, and these are said to be the source of misery. None can escape the effect of their own past karma. Once you free yourself from attachment you will see that</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->Live and allow others to live; hurt no one; life is dear to all living beings.</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->By sincerity, a man gains physical, mental and linguistic straightforwardness, and harmonious tendency; that is, congruence of speech and action.</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->All souls are equal and alike and have the similar nature and qualities.</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->Start the practice of self-control with some penance; begin with fasting.</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->The nature of things is dharma.</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->One who neglects or disregards the existence of earth, air, fire, water and vegetation disregards his own existence which is entwined with them.</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->Soul is the central point of spiritual discipline.</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->Eating constitutes the greatest obstacle to self-control; it gives rise to indolence.</li>
    <li>lessonReinforcement->No one can argue with that.</li>
  -->
  <AM_JainistDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <li>lesson(priority=-1)->事情发生了</li>
    <li>r_pattern->“[r_jainistlessonIntro][r_lesson]。[r_lessonReinforcement][r_jainlessonReinforcement]”\n\n  - [lessonAttribution]</li>
    <li>lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]，对[book]的[revision]</li>
    <li>lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]，对[book]的[revision]，[edition]</li>
    <li>lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull]，对经文的理解</li>
    <li>revision->解读</li>
    <li>revision->深入思考</li>
    <li>revision->性质剖析</li>
    <li>revision->思考</li>
    <li>revision->反思</li>
    <li>book->大雄教义</li>
    <li>book->《圣教论》</li>
    <li>book->经文合集</li>
    <li>book->先知经文</li>
    <li>edition->第三十二版</li>
    <li>edition->第四十三版</li>
    <li>edition->第五十二版</li>
    <li>edition->第五十七版</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->这是我的国家，那是你的国家；这些都是狭隘的灵魂才会萌生出的概念——对于自由主义者来说，整个世界就是一个家庭。我想让你明白： </li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->在快乐与痛苦之中，在欢乐与悲伤之中，我们应该像对待自己一样来对待所有生物。这教导我们</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->一些蠢货断言是造物主创造出了这个世界。认为世界是被创造出来的学说是欠佳考虑的，我们不该予以接受。如果说是神明创造了世界，那么在创造之前祂又身处何处呢？这种沉思确实教会了我一件事：</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->通过在[place_summary][place_name]上传授神圣的《圣教论》，我意识到</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->愿宇宙充满和平；愿国家充满和平；愿当权者能够实施和平统治；愿朋友的家中充满和平，愿敌人的家中也充满和平。平心而论，你会认识到</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->我们将时刻宣扬并实践手足情谊——无论是人类还是其他生物。我们始终相信普遍公平的法则。我们还将宣扬</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->如果一个人被复仇与嫉妒的力量冲昏了头脑，那他就无法向他人展现爱心与同情。有件事将会愈发明朗：那就是</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->在被烈火焚烧的森林中，有个人正盘坐在一棵树的顶端。他看见所有的生物都消亡殆尽了。但他并没有意识到同样的命运也会很快降临在他身上。那家伙就是个十足的蠢货。他只需要认识到</li>
    <li>jainistlessonIntro->爱慕与憎恶是业障的根本，而业障则源于痴迷。业障是生与死的根本，据传也是痛苦的源泉。没有人能逃脱自身过去业力的影响。一旦你从爱慕中解脱出来，你将会理解</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->众生皆应好好活着；不要伤害任何人；生命对众生而言都是无比珍贵的。</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->通过坦诚相待，一个人能够获得身体、心灵以及言语上的直率，以及对和谐向往；也就是说，人应做到言行一致。</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->所有的灵魂都是平等且相似的。</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->开始练习自我控制并忏悔吧；最好是从斋戒开始。</li>
    <li>jainlessonReinforcement->事物的本质即为法。</li>
